- Remove the `prematureText` variable entirely.
- Immediately record the trace after `visible` is computed.
- Push the assistant message onto `state.messages` (unchanged).
- Enter the `if (calls.length === 0)` branch.
  - First run the reality‑nudge logic exactly as before.
  - After that, if there is any visible text, emit it (no need to check `prematureText` because we already know there were zero calls, so any claim about an action would have been caught by the nudge guard).
- For the case where `calls.length > 0`, emit visible text only if it does not contain an action claim (`!claimsAction(visible)`). This ensures we don't prematurely say “I did X” before the tool actually runs.
- Keep the logging of `turn.done` and the return.

